From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Clay Stan <claystan97@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 22:25:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] cix: unlock sky1_init_mutex on PCIe power-enable timeout

In sky1_pcie_set_pwr_en(), the x2/x1 branch acquires sky1_init_mutex
before polling for the power-enable acknowledgement, but returned
-ETIMEDOUT directly on timeout while still holding the global mutex.
Unlock sky1_init_mutex before returning so a failed controller power-up
does not deadlock subsequent Sky1 PCIe operations.

Signed-off-by: Clay Stan <claystan97@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/pci/controller/cadence/pci-sky1-cix.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/cadence/pci-sky1-cix.c b/drivers/pci/controller/cadence/pci-sky1-cix.c
index 9c02fdf..618a25d 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/cadence/pci-sky1-cix.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/cadence/pci-sky1-cix.c
@@ -898,6 +898,7 @@ static int sky1_pcie_set_pwr_en(struct sky1_pcie *pcie, bool en)
 				sky1_pcie_set_bits32(strap_addr, 0x100);
 				ret = readl_poll_timeout(status_addr, read, !!(read&0x200), 5, 100);
 				if (ret) {
+					mutex_unlock(&sky1_init_mutex);
 					dev_err(dev, "Set pwr en err, 0x%x\n", read);
 					return -ETIMEDOUT;
 				}
